KG42.register("rules-ee9a8a0a8e372f45f6da040b",{"id":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction::v141-c-R006","paper":"15-multiagent_reverse_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The aggregator performs price-signal coordination by announcing the utility base price for the next hour's bid solicitation. Scope: Initial bid solicitation in the hour-ahead reverse auction for the grid-connected microgrid's lumped load. Price-signal updates are conditional on excess submitted supply: the aggregator lowers the price and requests new bids when supply exceeds demand. Scope: Iterative bidding in the hour-ahead reverse auction for the grid-connected microgrid's lumped load. Condition: Submitted supply exceeds demand.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E002","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.supply","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Initial bid solicitation in the hour-ahead reverse auction for the grid-connected microgrid's lumped load. | Iterative bidding in the hour-ahead reverse auction for the grid-connected microgrid's lumped load.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The aggregator performs price-signal coordination by announcing the utility base price for the next hour's bid solicitation. Scope: Initial bid solicitation in the hour-ahead reverse auction for the grid-connected microgrid's lumped load.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Price-signal updates are conditional on excess submitted supply: the aggregator lowers the price and requests new bids when supply exceeds demand. Scope: Iterative bidding in the hour-ahead reverse auction for the grid-connected microgrid's lumped load. Condition: Submitted supply exceeds demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g01-E17"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p04-c2r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"GAME THEORY 1067 Algorithm 1 Agent Negotiations Begin Initialize: All available generators register ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1 Agent Negotiations\nBegin\nInitialize: All available generators register to yellow page;\nLoop\nAggregator agent: inform utility base price, power demand for next hour;\nAggregator agent: request bids;\nif (DER base price \u003c utility base price) then\nBidder agents: inform submit bids;\nelse\nBidder agent: drop not participating;\nend"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"terminated. All available generators in the microgrid should 1) register to the yellow pages in orde","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"A reverse auction model has been implemented and realistically operated. Algorithm 1 briefly expresses the simplified pseudo code of the proposed reverse auction model. In Algorithm 1, the process is continuous unless the program is terminated. All available generators in the microgrid should register to the yellow pages in order to participate in bidding processes. The required amount of load is assumed to be correctly estimated for each upcoming hour; therefore the aggregator agent has this information ready to inform all agents registered to the yellow page. The main purpose of the aggregator agent is to purchase the required amount of energy with the least cost. The aggregator agent collects the submitted bids and checks whether the submitted supply matches the demand."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-1b3df4bc99-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Proposed Methodology","anchor_text":"terminated. All available generators in the microgrid should 1) register to the yellow pages in orde","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the supply is higher than the demand, the aggregator sends a new bidding request to the bidding agents by lowering the price. If bidding agents are still interested in the new submission, they submit the new price; otherwise they drop and quit from the auction for that particular hour. The process continues until only one qualified bidder remains in the auction."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The rule evidence describes coordination actions and a conditional response, but it does not define a decision variable symbol, domain, or optimization role for an operational variable. The price signal is represented as the prescribed graph node coordination.price_signal rather than as a typed variable.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed input or constant is defined as a symbol or parameter within this rule's evidence. The utility base price is mentioned as an announced price, but no general symbol, numeric value, or parameter domain is defined in the rule's C001/C002 evidence; example values and peak/regular utility prices occur in adjacent context."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E12","quote":"Aggregator agent: inform utility base price, power demand for next hour;\nAggregator agent: request bids;\nif (DER base price \u003c utility base price) then\nBidder agents: inform submit bids;"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E17","quote":"If the supply is higher than the demand, the aggregator sends a new bidding request to the bidding agents by lowering the price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","quote":"The aggregator agent collects the submitted bids and checks whether the submitted supply matches the demand."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"34bba78c5c4f47380b37d5df7a60566b18530cc480181658a49ae36e3dde0331","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"This rule is a procedural/logical coordination rule. The source states that the aggregator announces the utility base price and requests bids, and that when submitted supply exceeds demand it lowers the price and requests new bids. The supplied evidence does not define a quantitative price-signal variable, supply or demand symbols with domains, a general decrement formula, or an optimization expression for this rule. Utility price values and the 1-cent example decrement appear in adjacent examples/context, not as a formal rule-scope expression here. Existing graph nodes and edges suffice to represent the stated coordination and conditional relation.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"The local operator announces the utility base price as part of price-signal coordination; this is represented by the directed links edge from coordination.local_operator to coordination.price_signal."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E002"],"rationale":"The conditional price-lowering/new-bid action is governed by whether submitted supply exceeds demand, represented by the conditional_on edge from coordination.price_signal to bidding.supply."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
